WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:03.110
- Our next guest started his radio career

00:00:03.110 --> 00:00:06.010
in Los Angeles over 20 years ago,

00:00:06.010 --> 00:00:09.870
and has since become the voice of L.A.,

00:00:09.870 --> 00:00:12.330
and just last week, he became

00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:15.130
a permanent part of L.A. history,

00:00:15.130 --> 00:00:18.973
by receiving his star on
the Hollywood Walk of Fame.

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:24.683
Please welcome, Big Boy.

00:00:26.046 --> 00:00:28.796
(crowd applauds)

00:00:36.701 --> 00:00:37.534
- It is my pleasure to be here.

00:00:37.534 --> 00:00:39.231
- We are so honored.

00:00:39.231 --> 00:00:41.160
- Thank you, thank you.

00:00:42.223 --> 00:00:43.223
Hello there.

00:00:45.357 --> 00:00:47.440
- Did you ever think that you would

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:51.100
have a star on the Hollywood Walk of Fame?

00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:51.933
- No.

00:00:51.933 --> 00:00:55.900
You know, as a kid growing
up, I never thought of that.

00:00:55.900 --> 00:00:57.820
You know, I've been to Hollywood.

00:00:57.820 --> 00:00:59.380
Hollywood is one of those places where

00:00:59.380 --> 00:01:01.690
you walk down the street
and you look at those stars,

00:01:01.690 --> 00:01:04.600
but I've never walked down
the Boulevard and said,

00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:06.250
I'm going to have one of those.

00:01:06.250 --> 00:01:08.420
You know, as a kid growing up Drew,

00:01:08.420 --> 00:01:11.460
I was like, I had big dreams and

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:12.450
I would always tell my mom,

00:01:12.450 --> 00:01:13.890
I would say, oh mom, you know,

00:01:13.890 --> 00:01:15.340
one day I'm going to be famous.

00:01:15.340 --> 00:01:16.810
One day, I'm gonna sign autographs,

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:19.183
and my mom never deflated anything.

00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:23.270
We were homeless and as seven kids,

00:01:23.270 --> 00:01:25.320
my mom and I told her, I said, mom,

00:01:25.320 --> 00:01:26.830
one day, I'm gonna buy you a house

00:01:26.830 --> 00:01:28.980
so you won't have to be,
we won't be evicted again.

00:01:28.980 --> 00:01:31.020
She said, baby, I know you will.

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:33.660
And I felt like I wanted to be the person

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:36.760
that took care of my mom
and took care of my family.

00:01:36.760 --> 00:01:38.600
And when I got into radio,

00:01:38.600 --> 00:01:40.270
I was able to buy her that house

00:01:40.270 --> 00:01:41.600
that I told her I would purchase her

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:42.850
when I was a kid.

00:01:42.850 --> 00:01:44.693
She never got, you know,

00:01:44.693 --> 00:01:45.526
(crowd applauds)

00:01:45.526 --> 00:01:46.850
Thank you, thank you.

00:01:46.850 --> 00:01:49.210
- I've followed your career my whole life,

00:01:49.210 --> 00:01:52.300
because I listened to you on the radio.

00:01:52.300 --> 00:01:55.130
What was that first gig like?

00:01:55.130 --> 00:01:57.500
What was it like to hit the big time?

00:01:57.500 --> 00:02:00.510
And can you talk about
the music of that time?

00:02:00.510 --> 00:02:05.510
Because that also is so much
a part of the DNA of who I am.

00:02:06.778 --> 00:02:07.611
- Right.

00:02:07.611 --> 00:02:10.770
- That time is one of the best times,

00:02:10.770 --> 00:02:13.010
I believe, in music history.

00:02:13.010 --> 00:02:14.030
- Yeah, yeah.

00:02:14.030 --> 00:02:18.490
Getting into, getting into radio for me,

00:02:18.490 --> 00:02:21.170
I started at Power 106 in 1994.

00:02:21.170 --> 00:02:22.960
I knew some guys by the
name of The Baker Boys.

00:02:22.960 --> 00:02:25.370
You probably remember The Baker
Boys, early in the morning.

00:02:25.370 --> 00:02:27.550
And with The Bakers, I was just friends

00:02:27.550 --> 00:02:29.370
and I never thought, oh let me, you know,

00:02:29.370 --> 00:02:31.040
I can get a job here. I can get a job.

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:32.530
Their boss called me up one day

00:02:32.530 --> 00:02:34.050
and asked me if I wanted to try radio

00:02:34.050 --> 00:02:38.520
for one night, four hours, $35 an hour.

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:39.440
I'm thinking like, oh, okay.

00:02:39.440 --> 00:02:41.260
I'm just doing the math, not the career.

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:42.093
I'm doing the math.

00:02:42.093 --> 00:02:43.180
Like, okay, well what's that a hundred?

00:02:43.180 --> 00:02:44.013
Okay.

00:02:44.013 --> 00:02:44.846
And I do the math.

00:02:44.846 --> 00:02:47.680
I go, I get the second night
he calls me the next day.

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:48.880
I get the second day.

00:02:48.880 --> 00:02:52.130
Now at this time Drew
I'm over at that time,

00:02:52.130 --> 00:02:54.600
I'm probably like 450, 500 pounds.

00:02:54.600 --> 00:02:56.010
That's where the name Big Boy comes from.

00:02:56.010 --> 00:02:57.940
I was over 500 pounds.

00:02:57.940 --> 00:02:58.773
- [Drew] That's right.

00:02:58.773 --> 00:03:00.230
- And so I thought about it and I said,

00:03:00.230 --> 00:03:01.920
well, let me just try this radio thing.

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:06.517
So I went and tried radio
and that was 27 years ago.

00:03:06.517 --> 00:03:09.267
(crowd applauds)

00:03:11.466 --> 00:03:13.470
And with the music, I
was a fan of the music.

00:03:13.470 --> 00:03:17.930
So in 1994, I'm going in
playing people that's from L.A.,

00:03:17.930 --> 00:03:20.930
I'm playing Snoop Dogg,
I'm playing Dr. Dre,

00:03:20.930 --> 00:03:22.710
I'm playing Ice Cube.

00:03:22.710 --> 00:03:25.940
- You know, that was the time of music,

00:03:25.940 --> 00:03:30.050
and even earlier, like I was
really into Grandmaster Flash,

00:03:30.050 --> 00:03:32.860
I was really into Strafe, Monie Love,

00:03:32.860 --> 00:03:36.480
Slick Rick, EPMD, Public Enemy.

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:37.880
- Oh, you got a hip hop card.

00:03:37.880 --> 00:03:38.890
- Oh, I mean,

00:03:38.890 --> 00:03:40.150
- If we moved this out the way,

00:03:40.150 --> 00:03:42.600
she probably start pop
locking and break dancing.

00:03:44.040 --> 00:03:46.860
- This, this is what we grew up on.

00:03:46.860 --> 00:03:49.340
And it's, it formed me.

00:03:49.340 --> 00:03:52.230
And I liked putting images to music,

00:03:52.230 --> 00:03:55.220
and as a filmmaker and a producer,

00:03:55.220 --> 00:03:57.560
and certainly we fell in love with

00:03:57.560 --> 00:04:01.080
a director named McG who
had no credits to his name

00:04:01.080 --> 00:04:02.920
except for music videos.

00:04:02.920 --> 00:04:05.570
And I went to Sony pictures
and I was like, you know,

00:04:05.570 --> 00:04:07.060
as kids that you're trusting your

00:04:07.060 --> 00:04:09.470
hundred million dollar
Charlie's Angels movie with,

00:04:09.470 --> 00:04:11.710
well, we'd love this guy to direct it.

00:04:11.710 --> 00:04:13.800
His name is McG and they're like,

00:04:13.800 --> 00:04:15.460
he has done music videos.

00:04:15.460 --> 00:04:16.840
And I was like, I know,
and he's the only one

00:04:16.840 --> 00:04:20.370
who gets the tone of the
movie we want to make.

00:04:20.370 --> 00:04:23.100
And I'm so proud to say

00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:25.439
that you are in one of
the Charlie's Angels.

00:04:25.439 --> 00:04:26.272
- Yes I am.

00:04:26.272 --> 00:04:27.105
- You're in Full Throttle.

00:04:27.105 --> 00:04:29.020
We have a photo of it right here.

00:04:29.020 --> 00:04:29.853
- [Big Boy] Hello.

00:04:29.853 --> 00:04:33.146
- And just, it was so fun
to work with you then.

00:04:33.146 --> 00:04:33.979
- Thank you.

00:04:33.979 --> 00:04:35.585
- It's a pleasure to be with you now.

00:04:35.585 --> 00:04:36.418
- Thank you.

00:04:36.418 --> 00:04:39.570
- Congratulations on your
star on the Walk of Fame,

00:04:39.570 --> 00:04:42.398
the streets that you walked on.

00:04:42.398 --> 00:04:43.231
- [Big Boy] Thank you.

00:04:43.231 --> 00:04:44.780
- With hopes and dreams,

00:04:44.780 --> 00:04:47.810
proving that hopes and
dreams do come true.

00:04:47.810 --> 00:04:50.050
And we also know that
you just had a birthday

00:04:50.050 --> 00:04:52.170
and to celebrate your birthday,

00:04:52.170 --> 00:04:53.867
we have a little something for you.

00:04:53.867 --> 00:04:54.700
- Uh oh.

00:04:54.700 --> 00:04:56.953
Uh oh, uh oh.

00:04:57.819 --> 00:04:58.652
Thank you.

00:04:58.652 --> 00:05:02.096
- [Drew] I'm just gonna hold it up.

00:05:02.096 --> 00:05:02.929
- Man.

00:05:05.385 --> 00:05:07.480
Thank you so much.

00:05:07.480 --> 00:05:11.739
- I just want to say I'm so happy for you.

00:05:11.739 --> 00:05:12.572
- Thank you.

00:05:12.572 --> 00:05:15.190
- And I've just been one of
your biggest fans for so long.

00:05:15.190 --> 00:05:17.158
- I have been a big fan of yours as well.

00:05:17.158 --> 00:05:17.991
- Oh, thank you.

00:05:17.991 --> 00:05:18.824
- You know that.

00:05:18.824 --> 00:05:19.657
Like for real.

00:05:19.657 --> 00:05:20.490
- Thank you.

00:05:20.490 --> 00:05:21.323
Oh my gosh.

00:05:21.323 --> 00:05:22.630
I'm just, this is so fun for me.

00:05:22.630 --> 00:05:24.570
Okay, Big Boy, congratulations

00:05:24.570 --> 00:05:26.200
and happy birthday to you.

00:05:26.200 --> 00:05:29.700
Be sure to check out Big Boy's new show,

00:05:29.700 --> 00:05:32.760
After Hours With Big Boy

00:05:32.760 --> 00:05:37.131
starting on October 7th on
a new platform, Looped In.

00:05:37.131 --> 00:05:39.631
(theme music)

